Fillets: where the computation stopped when it is not done.

A fillet that is not done tells its faulty contours and their status
(StripeStatus) and its faulty vertices, but not at which stage it stopped:
a contour's blend can fail in its first section (StartsolFailure), in the
walk between its two faces or in a walk rolling on an edge (both
WalkingFailure), with a twisted surface, or with an exception (Error); the
stripes of blends that overlap or cross on a face can fail when they are
computed again; the check that the blends of two contours do not
intersect each other (ChFi3d_StripeEdgeInter) marks a stripe faulty whose
status stays Ok; and a corner can be built in part only (HasResult).
ChFi3d_Builder::Failure() now gives the stage (FailureKind) and
FailedContour() the contour it stopped at, also through
BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet. A walk rolling on an edge (the PerformSurf
variants with a restriction) is told from the walk between two faces by
the builder's own flag set where those walks fail. The computation itself
is unchanged.
